# Rank 1519 / CVE-2023-28326: OpenMeetings' invitation dialog enabled
# its personal-URL generate button whenever exactly one recipient was
# selected, without checking who the recipient was, so an inviter
# could generate a personal access URL for an ordinary user and
# bypass the intended permission path (broken access control,
# CWE-863; OPENMEETINGS-2739). updateButtons in
# openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/common/
# InvitationForm.java did `dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(recpnts.
# size() == 1)` -- the condition covers the count but not the
# principal: generating a URL is legitimate only for the inviter's
# own account or a CONTACT-type user. Pool commit 1fb71af36 is the
# real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "[OPENMEETINGS-2739] generate URL is
# disabled if non-contact is selected"): generateEnabled starts
# false and turns true only when the single recipient satisfies
# `getUserId().equals(u.getId()) || User.Type.CONTACT ==
# u.getType()`. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, capability-gate completeness. The guard exists and runs
# -- its condition names the wrong principal vocabulary (count, not
# type/identity), the same decision-completeness family as ranks
# 1540 (permission-switch branches), 1556 (sibling route groups) and
# 1567 (submit paths without the form token): nothing can ask "does
# the enabled-state condition of a capability cover the principal
# types allowed to exercise it" -- UI component state is not
# authorization vocabulary anywhere in the corpus. A binding on
# OpenMeetings' own dialog would detect this application rather than
# the weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning
# InvitationForm.java reports zero findings at both revisions. No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the piece is ontology design
# (capability-gate completeness), not a localised construct. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1519 records the
# count-only condition and the principal-checked form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-079: when capability-gate vocabulary
# lands, the count-only form must flip to expect.

test "rank1519: the generate button trusts the count alone"
  lang java
  file openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/common/InvitationForm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.openmeetings.web.common;

  import java.util.Collection;

  public abstract class InvitationForm extends Form<Invitation> {
      protected void updateButtons(AjaxRequestTarget target) {
          Collection<User> recpnts = recipients.getModelObject();
          target.add(
                  dialog.getSend().setEnabled(!recpnts.isEmpty())
                  , dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(recpnts.size() == 1)
                  );
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1519: the fix gates the button on the principal"
  lang java
  file openmeetings-web/src/main/java/org/apache/openmeetings/web/common/InvitationForm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.openmeetings.web.common;

  import java.util.Collection;

  public abstract class InvitationForm extends Form<Invitation> {
      protected void updateButtons(AjaxRequestTarget target) {
          Collection<User> recpnts = recipients.getModelObject();
          boolean generateEnabled = false;
          if (recpnts.size() == 1) {
              User u = recpnts.iterator().next();
              generateEnabled = getUserId().equals(u.getId()) || User.Type.CONTACT == u.getType();
          }
          target.add(
                  dialog.getSend().setEnabled(!recpnts.isEmpty())
                  , dialog.getGenerate().setEnabled(generateEnabled)
                  );
      }
  }
  ```
